f Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n1641,PANCREATITIS AGUDA,\"\"\"PANCREATITIS AGUDA\"\" refers to acute pancreatitis, a medical condition characterized by sudden inflammation of the pancreas. This condition can lead to severe abdominal pain and requires immediate medical attention. It is often associated with complications such as hyperglycemia and can necessitate careful nutritional management, particularly in diabetic patients. \n\nAcute pancreatitis may require nutritional support, which can include enteral nutrition or parenteral nutrition, especially during the initial days of treatment. The severity of the condition can vary, being classified as mild, moderate, or severe, depending on the presence of complications and organ failure. Symptoms typically manifest between 24 to 36 hours after the peak production of cytokines, and the condition is marked by elevated levels of pancreatic enzymes such as amylase and lipase in the blood.\n\nAcute pancreatitis is a common reason for emergency consultations, with a presentation rate of 0.1% to 1.5% in large hospitals. It is crucial for patients experiencing this condition to receive intensive treatment and monitoring to manage the potential complications effectively.\",54\r\n6839,DIGESTIVO,\"The DIGESTIVO service is dedicated to managing patients with gastrointestinal disorders, particularly those related to nutrition. This service is consulted for the endoscopic placement of enteral feeding tubes for patients, ensuring that individuals with specific dietary needs receive appropriate nutritional support.\",3\r\n2203,SÍNDROME DE RESPUESTA INFLAMATORIA SISTÉMICA,\"The \"\"Síndrome de Respuesta Inflamatoria Sistémica\"\" (Systemic Inflammatory Response Syndrome, SIRS) is a clinical condition that can arise from various severe clinical insults, including acute pancreatitis. It is characterized by a systemic inflammatory response, which may manifest through various clinical signs. In severe cases of pancreatitis, SIRS can lead to a hypermetabolic state, necessitating careful nutritional management to support the affected individual. Additionally, it has been noted that the condition can be mitigated through immunonutrition, particularly in post-surgical patients. Overall, SIRS represents a significant clinical challenge that requires comprehensive management strategies to address its inflammatory and metabolic implications.\",2\r\n3079,PROTEÍNA C REACTIVA,\"C-reactive protein (CRP), known in Spanish as \"\"Proteína C Reactiva,\"\" is a substance synthesized in the liver that serves as a marker of general inflammation. It reflects the body's nutritional status and is particularly relevant in assessing inflammatory conditions. Elevated levels of CRP are commonly observed in frail elderly individuals, indicating a potential risk of fragility in this population. Additionally, CRP is utilized in the nutritional assessment of burn patients, highlighting its importance in various clinical contexts related to inflammation and nutritional health.\",6\r\n7314,CÁNCER PANCREÁTICO,\"Cáncer pancreático, or pancreatic cancer, is a serious type of cancer that has been the subject of various studies exploring its potential links to dietary factors. Research has investigated the relationship between fish consumption and the incidence of pancreatic cancer, although findings may vary. Additionally, the connection between pancreatic cancer and dietary fiber intake, particularly from whole grains, remains inconsistent according to existing studies. This type of cancer is also noted for its impact on patients' metabolic rates, as it can increase resting energy expenditure. Furthermore, it is crucial to consider pancreatic cancer as a possible diagnosis in patients presenting with pancreatitis, especially when the underlying cause is not clearly identified.\",4\r\n6852,LITIASIS BILIAR,\"LITIASIS BILIAR, also known as biliary lithiasis or gallstones, is a significant medical condition characterized by the formation of stones in the bile ducts. It is recognized as the most common cause of acute pancreatitis in various countries, accounting for approximately 35% of episodes. This condition can arise as a complication of obesity, which negatively impacts digestive health and necessitates appropriate management. In particular, biliary lithiasis is one of the most prevalent etiologies of acute pancreatitis, as the presence of gallstones can obstruct the pancreatic duct, leading to inflammation and other serious complications.\",3\r\n3690,CITOCINAS,CITOCINAS son proteínas que desempeñan un papel crucial en la comunicación celular. Estas moléculas son fundamentales para influir en la inflamación y la respuesta inmune del organismo.,2\r\n2310,FALLO MULTIORGÁNICO,\"FALLO MULTIORGÁNICO is a medical condition characterized by the failure of multiple organ systems. This condition can arise as a complication of severe acute pancreatitis, where the inflammatory process affects various organs. Additionally, FALLO MULTIORGÁNICO can also occur in patients who have suffered severe burns, leading to the impairment of multiple body systems. The condition highlights the critical nature of organ function and the interconnectedness of bodily systems in response to severe medical stressors.\",2\r\n12254,ALGORITMO DEL MANEJO NUTRICIONAL,El algoritmo del manejo nutricional de la pancreatitis aguda es una guía adaptada para el tratamiento nutricional de pacientes con esta condición.,1\r\n6826,APACHE SCORE,\"The APACHE score is a severity scoring system used to measure the severity of disease in patients, particularly in critical care settings.\",1\r\n1907,ATONÍA GÁSTRICA,\"ATONÍA GÁSTRICA refers to a condition characterized by the stomach's loss of ability to contract and empty properly. This condition can significantly impact digestion and the intake of food. It is particularly noted to occur in patients suffering from acute pancreatitis, where it complicates the digestive process.\",1\r\n6853,CONSUMO EXCESIVO DE ALCOHOL,\"El consumo excesivo de alcohol es una de las principales causas de pancreatitis aguda, contribuyendo al daño del tejido pancreático.\",1\r\n12251,CORTISOL PLASMÁTICO,\"A hormone that increases in response to stress, often elevated in patients with severe acute pancreatitis\",1\r\n12247,CRITERIOS DE ATLANTA,Los criterios de Atlanta son un conjunto de directrices utilizadas para clasificar la severidad de la pancreatitis aguda.,1\r\n12250,DISFUNCIÓN ORGÁNICA MÚLTIPLE,\"A condition where multiple organs do not function properly, often seen in severe cases of acute pancreatitis\",1\r\n3481,ENFERMEDADES AUTOINMUNES,\"Autoimmune diseases, referred to as \"\"ENFERMEDADES AUTOINMUNES,\"\" are conditions characterized by the immune system erroneously attacking the body's own tissues. Research suggests that vitamin D may have a role in the prevention of these diseases. Additionally, autoimmune diseases can be a potential cause of pancreatitis, which highlights the importance of excluding them during the diagnostic process.\",1\r\n2204,FALLO ORGÁNICO PERSISTENTE,,1\r\n12249,HIDRATACIÓN INTRAVENOSA,La hidratación intravenosa es un tratamiento utilizado en pacientes con pancreatitis aguda para mantener el equilibrio de líquidos y electrolitos.,1\r\n6854,HIDROELECTROLÍTICOS,\"Los desequilibrios hidroelectrolíticos son complicaciones comunes en pacientes con pancreatitis aguda, afectando su tratamiento y recuperación.\",1\r\n2202,NECESIDAD DE CIRUGÍA DE URGENCIA,\"Urgent surgical intervention may be required in cases of severe pancreatitis aguda, particularly when complications arise.\",1\r\n6855,NECROSIS DEL PARÉNQUIMA,\"La necrosis del parénquima pancreático puede ocurrir en casos severos de pancreatitis aguda, complicando el tratamiento y aumentando el riesgo de mortalidad.\",1\r\n12248,OBSTRUCCIÓN PARCIAL DEL DUODENO,\"La obstrucción parcial del duodeno puede ser una complicación de la pancreatitis aguda, afectando la alimentación y la absorción 